ur sheet pan  and just take and spread  your  whipped cream throughout the sheet pan  like so and then get some food coloring  now what we're gonna do is put a few  drops  like so we'll use all different kind of  colors i've got pink and purple  just get have fun with it  let me put a few different colors okay  so i'm putting my last color on here  we're going to go green just as many  colors you want but don't do too much  because if you end up mixing too many  colors it just turns into a just purpley  brownish mess take a toothpick and just  start to swirl this around kind of  marble it  so this is something the kids will just  love just they can get dirty and have  fun and they can see the eggs and what  they do but just mix it around like so  put that aside and then just take those  eggs that are dry and put them in our  mix here and then we're just going to  roll them around  until they're completely covered so this  is as you can see you need to have  gloved hands because it makes a mess but  that's okay so get them all covered and  then they're going to sit  for 15 minutes  after those 15 minutes i'll show you  what happens you actually have to rinse  them off  so after those 15 minutes pass  then you rinse them off and then what  you end up with  is these beautiful tie dyed eggs look at  that really cool huh  so what i'm going to do is just put them  in our wonderful little easter basket  and we're ready for easter ready for the  bunny to hide these things  but either way  super fun and  you can find all these ingredients at  your local smiths thank you so much for  watching thank you for shopping and  we'll see you next time bye everybody  thank you again to smith's food and drug  for sponsoring this segment for more  information you can visit the website  that's right there on your screen  smithsfoodanddrug.com
 

